WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.432
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.432 --> 00:00:04.419
Today's message is do what you love.

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:06.610
Over to you, Ivanka Trump.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.725
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:11.120
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.616
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.616 --> 00:00:17.116
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:21.820
- I look around at my
girlfriends and at my guy friends

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.207
and they're in jobs that
they don't really have

00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:26.432
a lot of growth potential
and that they're not

00:00:26.432 --> 00:00:28.895
passionate about, and I think
if we're ever going to make

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.622
bold decisions, it has to be
at this point in our life.

00:00:31.622 --> 00:00:32.681
You know, we have to be out there,

00:00:32.681 --> 00:00:35.303
we have to be experimenting,
we have to be looking

00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:37.100
for that which makes us tick,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.293
and I think a big part
of that evolution for me

00:00:39.293 --> 00:00:42.939
was really, summer jobs and working

00:00:42.939 --> 00:00:45.946
and making sure to actually,
you know, get into the world,

00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:48.098
and try different things
and eliminate those

00:00:48.098 --> 00:00:50.815
which is as useful,
eliminating those career paths

00:00:50.815 --> 00:00:53.695
that you're not interested
in, as it is, you know,

00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:56.031
doing things that do interest you.

00:00:56.031 --> 00:00:59.243
But I think just being
bold and taking risks

00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:02.122
when you're young is so
important because I can't imagine

00:01:02.122 --> 00:01:04.289
working the hours that I do

00:01:04.289 --> 00:01:06.569
if I didn't fundamentally love it.

00:01:06.569 --> 00:01:08.409
And I think that's the
difference between somebody's

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:12.060
successful and somebody
that's extremely successful.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.825
Somebody that's good and somebody
that's exceptionally good

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:17.558
is the level of drive,

00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:19.823
which directly stems from passion.

00:01:19.823 --> 00:01:23.961
- So this message has to be
the most repeated message

00:01:23.961 --> 00:01:28.472
that I hear over and over
and over and over again

00:01:28.472 --> 00:01:30.625
from people who have had success.

00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:33.477
And success in general,
not just as entrepreneurs.

00:01:33.477 --> 00:01:36.580
I started off this channel
only focusing on entrepreneurs

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.341
and we branched out and
we've looked at athletes,

00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:41.141
and we've looked at musicians,
we've looked at singers,

00:01:41.141 --> 00:01:43.252
we've looked at artists,
we've looked at inventors.

00:01:43.252 --> 00:01:46.121
And consistently, across everybody

00:01:46.121 --> 00:01:47.953
who's reached the top of their game,

00:01:47.953 --> 00:01:51.012
the thing that they always say, always

00:01:51.012 --> 00:01:54.005
is you have to do what you love.

00:01:54.005 --> 00:01:55.866
- To do something that I love doing.

00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:57.122
- I love building teams.

00:01:57.122 --> 00:01:59.447
- Love the process of
solving the problems.

00:01:59.447 --> 00:02:01.483
- That's how much love I have
for this thing that I do.

00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:03.353
- I love every minute of it.

00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:04.431
- Really love to do it.

00:02:04.431 --> 00:02:06.244
- Get involved in things that you love.

00:02:06.244 --> 00:02:08.195
- You're so passionate,
excited, and in love with.

00:02:08.195 --> 00:02:10.504
- And you may have heard
that message before

00:02:10.504 --> 00:02:12.641
and you may say that that's boring

00:02:12.641 --> 00:02:16.148
and it's not interesting and
I already know that, Evan,

00:02:16.148 --> 00:02:17.537
but are you doing it?

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:18.950
'Cause the next part comes into

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.387
how do I find what I'm passionate about?

00:02:21.387 --> 00:02:23.402
How do I find the thing that I love?

00:02:23.402 --> 00:02:28.387
And this is where so
many people fall down.

00:02:28.387 --> 00:02:32.465
You find what you love
by exploring, by testing,

00:02:32.465 --> 00:02:35.420
by trying, by when you
get an idea for something,

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.960
you don't sit on it for five years

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.164
and hope one day it's going to happen.

00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:43.368
You find some small way
to get started, anything.

00:02:43.368 --> 00:02:47.204
An idea pops into your head,
find a small way to get started

00:02:47.204 --> 00:02:49.480
and see if it makes you come alive or not.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.651
If you want to open a snowboarding school,

00:02:51.651 --> 00:02:53.719
maybe you should learn how
to snowboard first, right?

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:57.595
And you can go and learn how
to snowboard right now, go.

00:02:57.595 --> 00:03:01.607
Pick up a snowboard, rent
it, go take a lesson and see.

00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:02.804
Does it make you come alive?

00:03:02.804 --> 00:03:04.639
Do you want to keep
doing this thing or not?

00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:06.340
Instead of making this
list of all these things

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.422
that one day you're going
to get to and never do.

00:03:08.422 --> 00:03:11.085
'Cause what ends up
happening is you settle.

00:03:11.085 --> 00:03:12.109
You settle.

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:14.979
You have ideas for what to do.

00:03:14.979 --> 00:03:17.715
You never actually go
out and do a lot of them.

00:03:17.715 --> 00:03:22.067
And what you're in, is
okay, it's pretty good.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:26.608
The enemy of greatness is not crap.

00:03:26.608 --> 00:03:28.418
It's not terrible.

00:03:28.418 --> 00:03:31.833
The enemy of greatness is good.

00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:34.452
Your situation right now,
yeah, it could be better

00:03:34.452 --> 00:03:37.243
but could be a lot worse too, you're good.

00:03:37.243 --> 00:03:40.121
You're good, so you don't
have the hustle and drive

00:03:40.121 --> 00:03:41.322
to go for great.

00:03:41.322 --> 00:03:43.151
That's where a lot of people fall down.

00:03:43.151 --> 00:03:44.881
I'd like to say that the
greatest basketball player

00:03:44.881 --> 00:03:47.573
of all time is not Michael Jordan,

00:03:47.573 --> 00:03:49.399
it's not Wilt Chamberlain,

00:03:49.399 --> 00:03:51.192
it's somebody who we've never heard.

00:03:51.192 --> 00:03:53.078
The greatest basketball of all time

00:03:53.078 --> 00:03:55.157
is a manager at Starbucks

00:03:55.157 --> 00:03:58.340
because he never picked up a
basketball 'cause he never knew

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.978
that he had that talent,
that passion, that ability

00:04:00.978 --> 00:04:03.620
'cause he didn't try,
'cause he settled too soon.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.035
He settled too early for okay

00:04:06.035 --> 00:04:07.477
and lives an okay life,

00:04:07.477 --> 00:04:10.203
instead of having Michael
Jordan level talent

00:04:10.203 --> 00:04:12.589
and dominating an industry.

00:04:12.589 --> 00:04:17.028
You have the ability to
dominate an industry.

00:04:17.028 --> 00:04:20.804
You have Michael Jordan
level talent at something

00:04:20.804 --> 00:04:23.555
that you will wake up
every day and want to crush

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:27.177
and go out and practice
and take shot after shot

00:04:27.177 --> 00:04:31.081
after shot and watch tape
and be obsessed with.

00:04:31.081 --> 00:04:33.207
You have that for something

00:04:33.207 --> 00:04:35.432
and if it's not for what
you're doing right now,

00:04:35.432 --> 00:04:37.534
then stop settling.

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:38.949
Stop mailing it in.

00:04:38.949 --> 00:04:41.190
Stop being okay with an okay life.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.583
You could do more and
not just for yourself.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.611
You could do more to
contribute to your family,

00:04:45.611 --> 00:04:46.586
to contribute to your community,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.158
to contribute to your country,

00:04:48.158 --> 00:04:50.491
to help the world with something.

00:04:50.491 --> 00:04:52.262
You have that ability,
that talent inside you,

00:04:52.262 --> 00:04:54.183
and what are you doing with it?

00:04:54.183 --> 00:04:55.668
If you are not that obsessed

00:04:55.668 --> 00:04:57.678
about what you're doing right now,

00:04:57.678 --> 00:04:59.579
I'm not saying drop it
immediately and just

00:04:59.579 --> 00:05:02.387
float and hope something comes.

00:05:02.387 --> 00:05:05.033
But you've had ideas, right?

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:07.290
You've had ideas of things to do.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.131
Stop sitting on them.

00:05:09.131 --> 00:05:11.191
Try it out.

00:05:11.191 --> 00:05:16.119
I never thought I would own
the largest salsa dance studio

00:05:16.119 --> 00:05:18.282
maybe in the world.

00:05:18.282 --> 00:05:19.828
I never thought it.

00:05:19.828 --> 00:05:21.385
I never thought about salsa dancing at all

00:05:21.385 --> 00:05:24.942
but I went to a salsa club

00:05:24.942 --> 00:05:28.390
and I liked it and I wanted to learn more,

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.644
and I wanted to do it
again, and do it again,

00:05:30.644 --> 00:05:32.538
and practice and get better and improve.

00:05:32.538 --> 00:05:35.119
One thing led to another and here we are.

00:05:35.119 --> 00:05:37.798
That's the story of a
lot of entrepreneurs.

00:05:37.798 --> 00:05:41.477
If you have an idea for
something, you owe it to yourself

00:05:41.477 --> 00:05:44.085
to give it a shot, to try it,

00:05:44.085 --> 00:05:48.001
to take some small step
and move it forward.

00:05:48.001 --> 00:05:49.767
And you may try it and hate it,

00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:51.251
and that's great information.

00:05:51.251 --> 00:05:53.813
Or you may try it and love
it and want to come back

00:05:53.813 --> 00:05:56.597
and do it again, and do
it again, and do it again.

00:05:56.597 --> 00:05:59.400
And if you find that thing
that you want to just

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.357
keep doing and keep grinding
and keep getting better at

00:06:02.357 --> 00:06:05.569
and keep improving, and
keep helping others with,

00:06:05.569 --> 00:06:07.076
that's the thing that you could have

00:06:07.076 --> 00:06:08.889
Michael Jordan level talent at

00:06:08.889 --> 00:06:11.888
and you owe it to yourself to go for it.

00:06:11.888 --> 00:06:14.431
So the question today, two parts.

00:06:14.431 --> 00:06:16.880
One, first part.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.993
If you know what you have
Michael Jordan level talent at,

00:06:20.993 --> 00:06:23.545
I want you to leave it
in the comments below.

00:06:23.545 --> 00:06:25.555
Part two, if you don't know what you have

00:06:25.555 --> 00:06:27.364
Michael Jordan level talent at,

00:06:27.364 --> 00:06:28.964
I want you to write down three things

00:06:28.964 --> 00:06:32.308
that you're going to start
to explore this week.

00:06:32.308 --> 00:06:35.464
That you've had ideas on
and you haven't done yet

00:06:35.464 --> 00:06:38.043
and you're going to try it out this week.

00:06:38.043 --> 00:06:40.576
Three ideas, leave it
in the comments below.

00:06:40.576 --> 00:06:42.991
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Scott Stokes

00:06:42.991 --> 00:06:45.267
from swainwoodham.co.nz.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:47.902
Thank you so much for picking
up a copy of my book, Scott,

00:06:47.902 --> 00:06:48.936
Your One Word.

00:06:48.936 --> 00:06:51.125
It really really really means a lot to me.

00:06:51.125 --> 00:06:52.719
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:52.719 --> 00:06:53.684
I believe in you,

00:06:53.684 --> 00:06:55.985
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:06:55.985 --> 00:06:58.200
And whatever your one word is

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.356
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:59.356 --> 00:07:01.776
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:01.776 --> 00:07:04.174
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:07.581
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:07:07.581 --> 00:07:09.573
Hey Believe Nation, we're
also looking at doing

00:07:09.573 --> 00:07:11.833
a top ten rules for success for Ivanka.

00:07:11.833 --> 00:07:13.433
Here is a sneak peek at some of the clips

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.362
that we're looking at.

00:07:14.362 --> 00:07:16.170
I hope you enjoy the bonus.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.022
- I think the only way to build confidence

00:07:18.022 --> 00:07:19.462
is through trial and error.

00:07:19.462 --> 00:07:21.488
I think when you're young,
one of the challenges

00:07:21.488 --> 00:07:24.852
is that you're insecure
about knowing nothing

00:07:24.852 --> 00:07:28.149
and you think people expect
you to have all the answers.

00:07:28.149 --> 00:07:31.541
Now, as a 34-year-old,

00:07:31.541 --> 00:07:34.176
I'm okay with not having all the answers.

00:07:34.176 --> 00:07:36.169
I recognize there's a lot I don't know

00:07:36.169 --> 00:07:38.340
and I own that and I love that

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:42.450
and it makes me curious and
helps me continue to grow.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.232
That's why I always tell
people, just get out

00:07:44.232 --> 00:07:45.160
and do things.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.746
You have to learn through trial and error,

00:07:46.746 --> 00:07:47.944
you have to just try.

00:07:47.944 --> 00:07:49.790
And every time you try something,

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:51.446
you get a little bit more experience,

00:07:51.446 --> 00:07:52.591
a little bit more wisdom,

00:07:52.591 --> 00:07:54.752
you build a little bit more confidence.

00:07:54.752 --> 00:07:56.935
So to all of you young
people, just get out there,

00:07:56.935 --> 00:07:59.304
start doing things, take risks,

00:07:59.304 --> 00:08:01.945
just, just try.

00:08:01.945 --> 00:08:03.795
- I ask all the women that I interview,

00:08:03.795 --> 00:08:05.631
can women truly have it all?

00:08:05.631 --> 00:08:07.537
Because when someone looks at your life

00:08:07.537 --> 00:08:08.585
from the outside in,

00:08:08.585 --> 00:08:10.832
you're a mother, you're a wife,

00:08:10.832 --> 00:08:12.667
you're a real estate developer,
you have a full time job,

00:08:12.667 --> 00:08:14.008
but you have another full time job

00:08:14.008 --> 00:08:15.197
because you also have a very

00:08:15.197 --> 00:08:17.724
successful clothing and
accessories business.

00:08:17.724 --> 00:08:19.291
So it seems like you have it all,

00:08:19.291 --> 00:08:21.486
but do you think women
really can have it all?

00:08:21.486 --> 00:08:23.943
- I think it's a very difficult question

00:08:23.943 --> 00:08:27.747
and it's one that I try not
to answer for other people

00:08:27.747 --> 00:08:30.883
because I think by its nature,

00:08:30.883 --> 00:08:32.637
what is having it all mean?

00:08:32.637 --> 00:08:34.700
It means different things
to different people.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.431
You know for me, it's very
important to have a family

00:08:37.431 --> 00:08:40.675
but it's also very important
to be professionally fulfilled.

00:08:40.675 --> 00:08:42.889
For some people, one of those is important

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:44.478
and the other isn't, so you know,

00:08:44.478 --> 00:08:46.946
I think you have to figure
out what your priorities are,

00:08:46.946 --> 00:08:49.960
in life are, and then architect your life

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.122
around those priorities.

00:08:52.122 --> 00:08:54.581
I think when people start to get lost,

00:08:54.581 --> 00:08:57.989
it's when their lives
are grossly inconsistent

00:08:57.989 --> 00:09:00.955
with their value set

00:09:00.955 --> 00:09:03.238
and their core priorities.

00:09:03.238 --> 00:09:05.715
So for me, you know at
the end of every week,

00:09:05.715 --> 00:09:07.939
I sort of do a self assessment of

00:09:07.939 --> 00:09:10.115
did I spend my time in the right way?

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:11.880
Was I where I needed to be?

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.322
You know, it's, there
are some days it's okay

00:09:14.322 --> 00:09:16.489
to not be home for dinner.

00:09:16.489 --> 00:09:19.599
If I have a big deal,
my priority may be that

00:09:19.599 --> 00:09:21.055
for that moment of time

00:09:21.055 --> 00:09:23.720
but I also know, if my
child ever gets sick,

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:27.030
if anything happens, well there
goes every other priority.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:30.235
So I think it's always a
balance, and you just have to do

00:09:30.235 --> 00:09:31.068
the best you can do.

